  "summary": "Dollar Store Vernacular is an aesthetic based around design that look and feel \"cheap\".",
  "description": "Dollar Store Vernacular is an aesthetic based around design that look and feel \"cheap\". These cheap designs are quickly produced for profit, leaving them with elements such as logos created using word art, poorly matching color combinations, and a large amount of cutout images. The aesthetic is often seen on things like travelling carnival signs, knock-off products, flyers, pop-up ads, firework packaging, bath salt packaging, etc.",
